  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Consider the quadratic form \n$Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+{x}_{3}^{2}.$ \nEvaluate $Q(x)$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$",
  "worked_solution": "We are given that \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the expression for $Q(x)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & ={1}^{2}-3\\cdot 1\\cdot (-4)-0\\cdot (-4)+(-4)^{2} \\\\  & =1+12+0+16 \\\\  & =29.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
